I read in the Object ID Spoiler that certain gems only begin to appear at
certain dungeon levels.  I decided to investigate the code, and figure it
out myself.  Afterwards, I compared the values I'd calculated with the
ones in the spoiler, and found a discrepancy of 1 -- the spoiler says new
gems appear at levels 4, 7, 10, ..., 28, while by my calculation the
levels are 3, 6, 9, ..., 27.

I rechecked my calculations, but I don't see how the spoiler could be
right.  The code (in o_init.c - setgemprobs()) bases the calculation on
the dungeon level's "ledger number" divided by three. The spoiler would be
correct if Dlvl:1 was ledger 0, but it looks to me that Dlvl:1 is indeed
ledger 1.


Also, there seems to be a harmless bug (dead code) in Nethack itself in
setgemprobs().  It contains the line:

lev = (ledger_no(dlev) > maxledgerno())
     ? maxledgerno() : ledger_no(dlev);

Which means to take either the ledger number or the maxledgerno() number,
and use whichever is lower.  But surely, maxledgerno() is never lower than
the current ledger number, so that code could be harmlessly shortened to
just:

lev = ledger_no(dlev);

Right?

